# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ── Node ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# ── Environment variables ─────────────────────────────────────
# Never commit a real .env — only the .env.example templates.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The virtualenv is a build artefact of requirements.txt, not source.
# It was tracked until 2026-09-01 (16,166 files) and has been untracked;
# recreate it with:
#   python3 -m venv ai-service/venv
#   ai-service/venv/bin/python -m pip install -r ai-service/requirements.txt
ai-service/venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# ── IDEs and editors ──────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
.DS_Store

# ── Playwright ────────────────────────────────────────────────
/playwright-report/
/test-results/

# ── Seed backups (rollback copies, regenerable) ───────────────
server/data/seed.js.pre-merge.bak
server/data/seed.js.pre-mombasa.bak
server/data/seed.js.pre-batch3.bak
server/data/seed.js.pre-batch4.bak
server/data/seed.js.pre-batch5.bak

# ── Pipeline intermediate/regenerable artifacts ───────────────
ai-service/pipeline/__pycache__/
ai-service/pipeline/counties/*/corpus/
ai-service/pipeline/counties/*/text/
ai-service/pipeline/_audit_check.py
ai-service/pipeline/seed_generated.js
ai-service/pipeline/seed_generated.json

# ── NOT ignored, deliberately ─────────────────────────────────
# ai-service/chroma_db/ is COMMITTED on purpose. It is regenerable
# (ai-service/ingest_all.py) but Render's free tier gives the container an
# ephemeral disk, so an index built after boot does not survive a cold start —
# which is how Audit AI ended up answering from a hand-written summary instead
# of the reports. Shipping the built index is what makes the corpus reliably
# present. Regenerate with `python ingest_all.py --force` when the PDFs change.
